cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ResolveLab or its published evidence, please cite it as below."
title: "ResolveLab: fault-injected tool environments with side-effect grading for agent evaluation and post-training"
type: software
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
authors:
  - family-names: Huang
    given-names: Allen
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ta0p1/ResolveLab"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agent evaluation
  - tool use
  - fault injection
  - imitation learning
  - API contract transfer
  - DAgger
  - LLM post-training
abstract: >-
  ResolveLab runs tool-using LLM agents against real HTTP services that inject failures
  (conflicts, rate limits, lost acknowledgements, revoked permissions, prompt injection) and
  grades episodes from server state and the commit log. Its registered studies, each with
  replayable evidence, test DAgger against a size-matched behaviour-cloning control (v0.4)
  and transfer to API dialects a model has never seen (v0.5).
